.TH HOWTO 1 "August 15, 2026" "HowTo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
howto \- turn plain English into a shell command locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howto
.RI [ options ] " request ..."
.br
.B howto
.RI command
.br
.B howto setup
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B HowTo
runs a local GGUF model through a llama.cpp engine compiled into the HowTo
binary and prints one shell command suited to the current platform. It targets
macOS with zsh and BSD tools first, and GNU/Linux with bash. Requests do not
leave the machine when using the default provider. Local mode needs no Python,
separate llama-server, local HTTP port, or Web UI.
.PP
Query generation requires the one-time
.B howto setup
workflow. Setup selects or preserves a profile, installs or reuses the model,
and can
configure context-aware Tab insertion for zsh, Bash, or fish. An interactive
query offers to start missing setup. Non-interactive queries fail with an
instruction instead of prompting or consuming request input.
.PP
When the shell integration is enabled, a successful single-result command
classified as NO_KNOWN_RISK or CAUTION is available once in that shell session.
Pressing Tab at a completely empty prompt inserts it into the editable buffer
without submitting it. Tab keeps its normal completion behavior otherwise.
Pending commands become unavailable after ten minutes. Bash integration
requires Bash 4.1 or newer; the default macOS zsh is supported.
.PP
The boolean
.B show_tab_hint
configuration setting defaults to true. Setting it to false suppresses only
the post-query reminder to press Tab; it does not disable Tab insertion or
prevent an eligible command from being offered at the next empty prompt.
.PP
The beta failed-command advisor is disabled by default. After a separate,
default-No opt-in, a compatible interactive shell sends only the raw text and
numeric exit status of a failed command to HowTo's embedded local model. HowTo
prints the suggested replacement as untrusted text and never executes, copies,
inserts, or stages it for Tab. The advisor captures no command output, current
directory, environment, directory listing, or file content and keeps no failed-
command history. Runtime acquisition and inference share a 20-second deadline.
It supports zsh and fish, plus Bash 5.1 and newer. When
.B server_url
is configured, the advisor is unavailable and sends nothing to that provider.
The Bash advisor also requires interactive command history to be enabled; it
does not create a separate history.
.PP
Advisor eligibility is limited to one literal external command no longer than
4096 bytes with an exit status from 1 through 127. Compound syntax, redirects,
expansions, wrappers, builtins, control characters, leading whitespace, and
secret-like text are skipped before inference. This filtering cannot identify
every sensitive value.
.PP
The words help and version select management commands when alone. Doctor
and setup select management parsing when alone or followed by an option. Model,
server, and config also select it when alone, or when followed by a documented
action or option. Shell requires a documented action or option.
Once selected, all remaining management arguments are validated strictly.
Use
.B --
to force query parsing for natural language with a management-shaped prefix.
.PP
Generated commands are not executed unless
.B --execute
is supplied and an interactive confirmation succeeds. Commands classified as
DANGER or UNKNOWN are never executed. The checker is a denylist and syntax
analyzer, not a sandbox; always review generated commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -x ", " -e ", " --execute
Execute the selected command after confirmation. Incompatible with
.B --json
and
.BR --quiet .
.TP
.BR -c ", " --copy
Copy the selected command to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quiet
Print only a command with no known risk. CAUTION, DANGER, and UNKNOWN output is
refused in this mode. Incompatible with
.BR --json ,
.BR --execute ,
and a count greater than one.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --count " " N
Generate up to N alternatives, from 1 through 8.
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured JSON.
.TP
.B --timing
Print generation timing to standard error.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Show the HowTo version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup [-y|--yes] [--model compact|balanced|accurate] [--no-shell|--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Perform or repair required onboarding. In local mode, select a published model
profile before downloading, resuming, and verifying its pinned artifact bundle.
Configured-provider mode skips the local model. By default, interactive setup
asks whether to install the Tab integration. Use
.B --yes
to accept default-Yes setup prompts,
.B --no-shell
to complete setup without integration and remove prior managed hooks, or
.B --shell
to choose an integration explicitly. Open a new terminal after enabling it.
Once compatible shell integration is successfully configured, interactive local
setup separately asks whether to enable the beta failed-command advisor with a
default answer of No. Neither
.B --yes
nor non-interactive setup implies that consent.
.TP
.B doctor [--json] [--deep]
Inspect setup, configuration, model, and resident embedded-engine status.
For a configured provider, try GET /health and then GET /v1/models, using the
configured bearer token when present; this does not test chat completion. In
local mode, report the runtime as embedded and do not load a model merely for
the diagnostic.
.TP
.B model [status] [--json] [--deep]
Inspect the installed model and optionally verify a managed or packaged copy
of the selected published catalog model against its pinned SHA-256 digest.
Custom models have no built-in expected digest.
.TP
.B model list [--json]
Compare Compact, Balanced, and Accurate catalog metadata and publication state.
.TP
.B model install [compact|balanced|accurate] [-y|--yes]
Download, resume, verify, atomically install, and select a published profile.
An unpublished profile fails before network access.
.TP
.B server [status] [--json]
Show resident embedded-engine status and any detected pre-upgrade
llama-server.
.TP
.B server stop [--json]
Stop only the embedded worker process recorded and validated as HowTo's. Also
clean up a recorded legacy llama-server when present.
.TP
.B shell status [--json]
Show whether shell integration is persistently configured and active in the
current shell.
.TP
.B shell enable [--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Install or repair the embedded adapter and marked startup-file blocks. Each
existing startup file is backed up before an atomic change. Bash manages both
.I ~/.bashrc
and its active login file. A safe symlink in a startup path requires a separate,
default-No interactive approval showing its resolved target and exact managed
block; unattended invocations do not follow it. Requires completed setup.
.TP
.B shell disable [--shell zsh|bash|fish]
Remove the selected or receipt-tracked managed startup blocks, adapter, and
pending command state.
.TP
.B shell init zsh|bash|fish
Print the embedded adapter. This is primarily a diagnostic and integration
surface; normal users should use
.BR "howto setup" .
.TP
.B config [list [--json]|path|get KEY|set KEY VALUE|unset KEY]
Inspect or update HowTo's JSON configuration. For example,
.B howto config set show_tab_hint false
hides only the post-query Tab reminder while leaving Tab insertion enabled.
Use
.B howto config set failed_command_advisor true
for an explicit advisor opt-in, and set it to false to disable automatic
suggestions without removing Tab insertion.
.TP
.B help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B version
Show the HowTo version and exit.
.SH MODEL PROFILES
Schema-1 upgrades retain the published
.B legacy
nl2sh 1.5B model and its old flat model path, avoiding another download.
When qualified entries are available, new interactive setup recommends
.BR balanced ;
.B --yes
selects that recommendation, and an existing installation can change profiles
with
.BR "model install PROFILE" .
.PP
The catalog currently describes three tuned research candidates:
.TP
.B compact
Qwen2.5-Coder 0.5B; 63.75 percent executable pass@1; 469 MiB reference disk;
86.4 ms research BF16 mean latency; 1.14 GB research accelerator peak;
provisional 1.5 GiB host-RAM guidance.
.TP
.B balanced
Qwen3.5 0.8B; 67.75 percent executable pass@1; 537 MiB reference disk;
180.0 ms research BF16 mean latency; 1.62 GB research accelerator peak;
provisional 2 GiB host-RAM guidance.
.TP
.B accurate
Qwen3.5 2B; 74.50 percent executable pass@1; 1332 MiB reference disk;
181.8 ms research BF16 mean latency; 3.96 GB research accelerator peak;
provisional 4 GiB host-RAM guidance.
.PP
Quality is from one 400-task held-out Linux/bash fold. Latency and peak memory
were measured in BF16 on an NVIDIA RTX 5090, not with final GGUFs on a Mac or
representative Linux host. All three profiles are currently unpublished and
not installable. Their Apache-2.0 base licenses do not by themselves clear the
tuned derivatives for distribution. The catalog activates a profile only after
redistribution clearance and immutable merged-GGUF URL, size, SHA-256,
prompt/stop, quality, Mac/Linux performance, and memory qualification.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration uses schema 2. Schema 1 is migrated with
.BR model_profile=legacy ;
schema 0, future schemas, and unknown keys are rejected. Select
.B model_profile
through setup or model install so verification precedes selection. Stored model
and shell paths must be absolute. The deprecated
.B llama_server_path
field is still parsed for migration but ignored by local inference. The
generation limit must be smaller than the configured context size. HTTP(S)
provider URLs may include a base path but cannot include credentials, a query,
or a fragment; Unix-socket provider paths must be absolute.
.PP
.B accelerator
accepts
.B auto
or
.BR cpu ,
defaults to auto, and can force the portable CPU path when native GPU or Metal
initialization is unavailable.
.PP
.B show_tab_hint
accepts true or false and defaults to true.
.B failed_command_advisor
also accepts true or false, defaults to false, and is effective only with
compatible shell integration and the embedded local provider. It cannot be true
while
.B server_url
is configured.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOWTO_HOME
Override all HowTo data directories with one absolute path. Relative paths
are rejected. Intended for tests and portable setups.
.TP
.B HOWTO_MODEL
Use a specific GGUF model file.
.TP
.B HOWTO_PACKAGED_MODEL
Add a package-provided default-model candidate.
.TP
.B HOWTO_LLAMA_SERVER
Deprecated and ignored by local inference. Retained so an old environment
cannot redirect the embedded engine during migration.
.TP
.B HOWTO_API_KEY
Bearer token for a configured external provider. It is removed from the
environment of a generated command approved for execution.
.TP
.B HOWTO_SHELL_SESSION
Internal non-secret per-shell identifier exported by the managed shell adapter.
Do not set it manually.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Linux directory overrides. A value must be absolute when set.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Runtime-state parent on macOS or Linux. A value must be absolute when set.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
System temporary-directory override used when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is absent. A
value used for runtime state must be absolute.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/HowTo
macOS configuration, setup receipt, models, and shell adapter.
.TP
.I ~/.config/howto and ~/.local/share/howto
Linux configuration, setup receipt, models, and shell adapter.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/howto or $TMPDIR/howto-UID
Private embedded-engine state and one-shot, session-scoped pending commands.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Logs/HowTo/engine.log
macOS embedded-engine log.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/howto/log/engine.log
Default Linux embedded-engine log; XDG_STATE_HOME can change its parent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
howto setup
howto model list
howto "free port 8080"
howto find files larger than 1GB
howto -x show my current IP address
howto doctor --deep
howto server status
howto shell status
howto config set failed_command_advisor true
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
indicates success.
.TP
.B 1
indicates an operational failure or an unsuccessful diagnostic/status check.
.TP
.B 2
indicates invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
indicates a configuration, dependency, or model error.
.TP
.B 4
indicates an embedded-engine, network, or model-response error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1)
